From: winglm port
Subject: [PATCH] gio: g_local_file_query_exists: fall back to lstat on EINVAL

glib 2.90 calls faccessat(AT_EACCESS | AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW). musl only
accepts AT_EACCESS and returns EINVAL, so g_file_query_exists() said FALSE
for every path on Alpine. libxmlb then tried to create the existing
appstream cache dir, appstream 1.2.1 double-freed the resulting GError and
phosh/phrog crashed at startup.
---
--- a/gio/glocalfile.c	2026-11-16 00:11:27.145677227 +0400
+++ b/gio/glocalfile.c	2026-11-16 00:11:27.184051666 +0400
@@ -1294,7 +1294,12 @@
     }
   else if G_UNLIKELY (errno == EINVAL)
     {
-      g_critical ("g_local_file_query_exists: faccessat doesn't support supplied flags");
+      /* musl's faccessat() only accepts AT_EACCESS and fails with EINVAL
+       * when AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW is passed. Answer the question with
+       * lstat() instead, like the fallback implementation does. */
+      GStatBuf buf;
+
+      return g_lstat (local->filename, &buf) == 0;
     }
 
   return FALSE;
